;;; subject: opendev-terminal-agent-2603 2.3.4 Context-Aware System Reminders: how short messages are injected just before the decision that would otherwise go wrong, so that early instructions keep their effect in a long run
;;; made-from: doc_Base012/docs/Papers-AgentHarness/opendev-terminal-agent/03_context-engineering/03_context-engineering.lisp / s19 .. s13
;;; members: problem example cause approach detectors templates guards user-role degradation design-evolution
;;; elsewhere: none
;;; left-out: the captions of Figures 11 and 12
(defrule reminders -> reminders-problem reminders-example reminders-cause reminders-approach reminders-detectors reminders-templates reminders-guards reminders-user-role reminders-degradation reminders-design-evolution)
(defrule reminders-problem -> :nucleus reminders-problem/n)
(defrule reminders-problem/n -> :instruction "長い実行で信頼性が下がる根本の問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "System reminders address a fundamental reliability problem in long-running agent sessions: as the conversation grows, the model’s attention drifts away from the initial system-prompt instructions, leading to silent failures such as premature task completion, abandoned error recovery, and unchecked exploration spirals (Figure 11).")
(defrule reminders-example -> :nucleus reminders-example/n :elaboration-additional reminders-example/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-example/a2)
(defrule reminders-example/n -> :instruction "指示が忘れられていく具体的な場面を 1 文で書く" :sample "Consider a coding agent that is told, in its system prompt, to always run tests after editing code.")
(defrule reminders-example/a1 -> :instruction "最初の数ターンと、その後の違いを 1 文で書く" :sample "For the first few turns, it does.")
(defrule reminders-example/a2 -> :instruction "同じ型の別の失敗を挙げて 1 文で書く" :sample "The same pattern appears in other forms: an agent told to “ finish all tasks before stopping ” declares victory with half the list incomplete; an agent that hits a file-editing error gives up instead of re-reading the file and retrying, even though its instructions say to retry.")
(defrule reminders-cause -> :nucleus reminders-cause/n :elaboration-additional reminders-cause/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-cause/a2)
(defrule reminders-cause/n -> :instruction "原因が指示文の位置にあることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The root cause is simple: the system prompt sits at the very beginning of the conversation.")
(defrule reminders-cause/a1 -> :instruction "指示が残っているのに効かなくなることを 1 文で書く" :sample "The rules are still present in the context window, but their influence fades with distance.")
(defrule reminders-cause/a2 -> :instruction "この失敗が再現することを 1 文で書く" :sample "This is not a hypothetical concern; it is a predictable, reproducible failure mode that we observed consistently in sessions exceeding 15 tool calls.")
(defrule reminders-approach -> :nucleus reminders-approach/n :elaboration-additional reminders-approach/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-approach/a2)
(defrule reminders-approach/n -> :instruction "全部を先頭に置く方式の限界を 1 文で書く" :sample "Putting all instructions up front works initially but degrades over long sessions.")
(defrule reminders-approach/a1 -> :instruction "指示文を繰り返し入れる方式の欠点を 1 文で書く" :sample "Re-injecting the entire system prompt every few turns wastes tokens on instructions the agent does not currently need.")
(defrule reminders-approach/a2 -> :instruction "採った方式と、その形を 1 文で書く" :sample "OpenDev addresses this with system reminders: short, single-purpose messages injected exactly when the agent needs them, right before the decision point where it would otherwise go wrong.")
(defrule reminders-detectors -> :nucleus reminders-detectors/n :elaboration-additional reminders-detectors/a1)
(defrule reminders-detectors/n -> :instruction "注入の層が監視する条件の数を 1 文で書く" :sample "As shown in Figure 12, the injection layer monitors eight conditions at the boundary between tool execution and the next LLM call: tool failure without retry (with six error-specific recovery templates), exploration spirals (5+ consecutive reads), denied tool re-attempts, premature completion with incomplete todos, continued work after all todos are done, plan approval without follow-through, unprocessed subagent results, and empty completion messages.")
(defrule reminders-detectors/a1 -> :instruction "検出された条件と雛形の対応を 1 文で書く" :sample "Each detector fires its corresponding reminder template from a catalog of named reminders organized into several categories: phase control, task lifecycle, todo enforcement, error recovery, behavioral correction, and JSON retry (Appendix F provides the full catalog and injection timing).")
(defrule reminders-templates -> :nucleus reminders-templates/n :elaboration-additional reminders-templates/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-templates/a2)
(defrule reminders-templates/n -> :instruction "雛形の文面が置かれる場所を 1 文で書く" :sample "All reminder text lives outside source code.")
(defrule reminders-templates/a1 -> :instruction "取り出しの手順を 1 文で書く" :sample "The entry point get_reminder(name, **kwargs) parses the file once into a module-level cache on first call, looks up the section by name, and fills placeholders (e.g., {count}, {todo_list}) via str.format().")
(defrule reminders-templates/a2 -> :instruction "平文で持つ利点を 1 文で書く" :sample "Keeping templates in plain text makes them auditable and editable without touching Python code.")
(defrule reminders-guards -> :nucleus reminders-guards/n :elaboration-additional reminders-guards/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-guards/a2 :elaboration-additional reminders-guards/a3)
(defrule reminders-guards/n -> :instruction "毎回出すと雑音になる問題を 1 文で書く" :sample "A reminder that fires on every iteration stops being helpful and becomes noise the model learns to ignore.")
(defrule reminders-guards/a1 -> :instruction "制限の仕組みを 1 文で書く" :sample "To prevent this, each reminder type is governed by a counter or a one-shot flag tracked in the per-session IterationContext (right column of Figure 12).")
(defrule reminders-guards/a2 -> :instruction "上限の具体値を 1 文で書く" :sample "Incomplete-todo nudges fire at most twice (MAX_TODO_NUDGES = 2); error-recovery nudges fire at most three times (MAX_NUDGE_ATTEMPTS = 3); plan-approved, all-todos-complete, and completion-summary signals each fire exactly once.")
(defrule reminders-guards/a3 -> :instruction "上限に達しても反応が無いときの扱いを 1 文で書く" :sample "If the agent does not respond to a capped nudge, the system accepts the agent’s judgment and moves on rather than looping.")
(defrule reminders-user-role -> :nucleus reminders-user-role/n :elaboration-additional reminders-user-role/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-user-role/a2)
(defrule reminders-user-role/n -> :instruction "催促を利用者の役割の発言として入れる方針を 1 文で書く" :sample "Reminders are injected as role: user messages rather than role: system.")
(defrule reminders-user-role/a1 -> :instruction "その理由を 1 文で書く" :sample "After 40 turns of conversation, another system message blends into the background that the model has already partially forgotten.")
(defrule reminders-user-role/a2 -> :instruction "実験で確かめたことを 1 文で書く" :sample "Early experiments with role: system injection confirmed this: user-role reminders produced noticeably higher compliance rates.")
(defrule reminders-degradation -> :nucleus reminders-degradation/n :elaboration-additional reminders-degradation/a1)
(defrule reminders-degradation/n -> :instruction "雛形が欠けたときもエージェントが動くことを 1 文で書く" :sample "If a reminder template is missing or retrieval fails, the agent still has its system prompt.")
(defrule reminders-degradation/a1 -> :instruction "催促が果たす役割の限界を 1 文で書く" :sample "Reminders reinforce existing instructions; they do not introduce new ones.")
(defrule reminders-design-evolution -> :nucleus reminders-design-evolution/n :elaboration-additional reminders-design-evolution/a1 :elaboration-additional reminders-design-evolution/a2)
(defrule reminders-design-evolution/n -> :instruction "初期の仕組みと、長い実行で出た失敗を 1 文で書く" :sample "The initial system relied entirely on the system prompt.")
(defrule reminders-design-evolution/a1 -> :instruction "誤りの種類を分けた効果と、制限を足す前の失敗を 1 文で書く" :sample "Early error recovery used a single generic “ try again ” message; classifying errors into six types with specific guidance substantially improved recovery rates, as “ read the file again ” is more actionable than “ fix the issue .” Before one-shot flags and attempt budgets, some reminders fired on every iteration, causing the agent to loop on the nudge itself; guards were essential for stability.")
(defrule reminders-design-evolution/a2 -> :instruction "指示文での注入の効果が低かったことを 1 文で書く" :sample "Early experiments also injected reminders as role: system messages, which were less effective because the model treated them as background instructions rather than conversational prompts demanding a response.")
